[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/336082657","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/1699#issuecomment-336082657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/1699","id":336082657,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzNjA4MjY1Nw==","user":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-10-12T10:04:54Z","updated_at":"2017-10-12T10:04:54Z","body":"This happens because we are inferring `current_process` as a staticmethod, coming from here: https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/master/Lib/multiprocessing/context.py#L37. We should check why the inference engine can't infer accessors such as this one as being callable. Th brain_multiprocessing plugin is here https://github.com/PyCQA/astroid/blob/9d94babb2e968c5a343218a48684a9529cbab568/astroid/brain/brain_multiprocessing.py, which just instantiates `BaseContext` and adds its members to the global namespace.\r\nBasically when the issue gets fixed, the following should not emit `Uninferable` as it does now, but rather the `current_process` function:\r\n\r\n```\r\nfrom astroid import extract_node\r\nn = extract_node('''\r\nfrom multiprocessing.context import BaseContext\r\nc = BaseContext()\r\nc.current_process\r\n''')\r\ni = next(n.infer())\r\nprint(i)\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/336082657/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":1289913323,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyODk5MTMzMjM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/events/1289913323","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2017-10-12T10:05:04Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"fc2929"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":1289913484,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyODk5MTM0ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/events/1289913484","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2017-10-12T10:05:09Z","label":{"name":"astroid","color":"ededed"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/361729258","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/1699#issuecomment-361729258","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/1699","id":361729258,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2MTcyOTI1OA==","user":{"login":"brycepg","id":441800,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MTgwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/441800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg","html_url":"https://github.com/brycepg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-01-30T20:48:32Z","updated_at":"2018-01-30T21:03:52Z","body":"I think there may be an easy workaround for this issue using `@staticmethod` in the multiprocessing brain and then opening up a separate issue in astroid for explicitly calling staticmethod\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHere's what I found about `staticmethod`: In Python, a function wrapped with staticmethod isn't inferable unless it's defined in a class namespace (and called after the namespace is fully created).\r\n\r\nHere's a Python code example of when staticmethod is / is not `Callable`:\r\n```python\r\ndef hi():\r\n    pass\r\nstaticmethod_instance_hi = staticmethod(hi)\r\nstaticmethod_instance_hi # Not Callable here\r\nclass Foo:\r\n    hi_staticmethod = staticmethod_instance_hi\r\n    print(hi_staticmethod) # Still not Callable\r\nFoo.hi_staticmethod() # Callable\r\nFoo().hi_staticmethod() # Callable\r\ndef a_function():\r\n    pass\r\na_function.a_function_attribute = staticmethod_instance_hi\r\na_function.a_function_attribute # not Callable\r\nfunc = Foo.hi_staticmethod\r\nfunc() # Callable\r\n```\r\n\r\nAstroid only infers `staticmethod`s correctly using the `@staticmethod` syntax (using this decorator it correctly infers the attribute as a function instead of a bound or unbound method.\r\n\r\nWhen explicitly calling staticmethod on a function in a class namespace (as in multiprocessing's case), astroid is either inferring the value as an instance of staticmethod (which is valid when not defined inside a class definition) or `Uninferable` (not sure why)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/comments/361729258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"brycepg","id":441800,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MTgwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/441800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg","html_url":"https://github.com/brycepg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycepg/received_events